from pathlib import Path
import json,html,base64
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;b=json.loads((R/'web-search/beat.json').read_text())
def image(name):return 'data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((R/'web-search'/name).read_bytes()).decode()
style='''<style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f7f5ef;color:#29323a;font:17px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1300px;margin:auto;padding:40px 28px}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.1;max-width:900px}h2{margin-top:44px}p{max-width:1050px}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #ddd}article{background:white;border:1px solid #dedbd2;padding:24px;margin:26px 0;border-radius:18px}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}small{color:#71684e}.pill{display:inline-block;padding:4px 12px;background:#ffe7cb;border-radius:20px}a{color:#8a472a}dt{font-weight:700;margin-top:12px}dd{margin-left:0;color:#545f66}@media(max-width:700px){.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}}</style>'''
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Image-first storyboard: web search</title>'+style+'<main><span class="pill">Design review · images before animation</span><h1>Design the explanation before building its motion.</h1><p>The earlier full-video render was rejected as a design-quality baseline. This pilot makes the intended appearance visible in three meaningful states, before any new animation is implemented.</p><p><b>Workflow:</b> transcript → teaching beat → generated master still → coherent state images → visual review → editable layers → still comparison → timed motion.</p><p>These images are proposed art direction, not approved final assets. Earlier states are image edits derived from the same settled master. The right-hand blank tile reserves presenter space.</p><p><b>Source correction:</b> The original introduces the model first, then adds the web input and result. These revised states follow that reveal order; the older web-only draft is archived.</p><h2>What the original does better</h2><div class="pair"><section><h3>Source at 01:57</h3><img src="'+image('source-reference.png')+'"></section><section><h3>Rejected baseline</h3><img src="'+image('rejected-baseline.png')+'"></section></div><p>The source has centered filled icons, serif labels, soft off-white surfaces, a warm peach focal card, semantic orange/green accents, shadows and breathing room. The failed version changes the visual language and even substitutes business-flow labels for this web-search example.</p><blockquote>'+html.escape(b['narration_excerpt'])+'</blockquote><p><b>Why this graphic:</b> '+html.escape(b['why_this_graphic'])+'</p>']
for i,s in enumerate(b['states']):
 parts.append(f'<article><small>STATE {i+1} OF 3 · {html.escape(s["id"])}</small><h2>{html.escape(s["new_understanding"])}</h2><img src="{image(s["image"])}"><dl><dt>Narration role</dt><dd>{html.escape(s["narration_role"])}</dd><dt>What remains stable</dt><dd>{html.escape(", ".join(s["persistent"]))}</dd><dt>Proposed transition</dt><dd>{html.escape(s["next_transition"])}</dd></dl></article>')
parts.append('''<h2>Visual review before animation</h2><p>Direction restored: warm semantic colors, centered icons and serif labels, subtle surface depth, clean directional arrows and fixed composition. These are candidate images: visual approval remains open.</p><p>Remaining reference differences to resolve: the source gives the model card more relative scale; generated shadows, label weight and gradient need comparison at the final player size. Earlier image edits can still change small color details, so the editable reconstruction must use one shared set of style tokens rather than copying pixels from independent frames.</p><h2>How this becomes motion</h2><p>Reconstruct the selected still with separate background, grid, card surfaces, gradients, shadows, icons, exact labels and connectors. Compare that editable still against the selected master. Animate those layers between the chosen states, aligned to narration, with deliberate settles and holds. A generated picture is the visual target; it is not an automatically editable animation.</p><p><b>Claim caveat:</b> The source's “Accurate Results” label describes its constrained-context example. It is not a universal model-accuracy guarantee. The next business-context counterexample must be storyboarded separately.</p><p><a href="PROCESS.md">Full process</a> · <a href="storyboard.json">Storyboard contract</a> · <a href="web-search/beat.json">Teaching beat and layer blueprint</a></p></main></html>''')
(R/'review.html').write_text(''.join(parts))
scene={'id':b['id'],'transcript':b['narration_excerpt'],'intended_understanding':b['intended_understanding'],'template_id':'failure-example','template_variant':'Constrained-context baseline before the business-context counterexample','reference_sequence':'04-context-problem','composition':'White faint grid; three fixed left-to-right card slots; warm peach model focal point; centered filled symbols and serif labels; independent reserved presenter tile.','assets':'Generated master still and two image edits, source reference and rejected baseline. Editable layers are specified but not yet implemented.','reason':b['why_this_graphic'],'alternative_and_tradeoff':b['alternative']+'. '+b['alternative_tradeoff'],'state_plan':'Model introduced → web input added → completed result flow. Earlier states derived from the selected candidate master. Actual motion alignment is pending.','clarity_check':'Review source versus candidate for typography, icon mass, card scale, shadow, spacing and continuity. Model-card relative scale remains a refinement; no visual approval asserted.','sources':[b['source_url']],'source_start':108,'source_end':119,'status':'assets_ready','master_image':'web-search/'+b['master_image'],'reference_library_entry':'../reference-library/entries/constrained-web-flow.json','reference_images':['../reference-library/'+x for x in json.loads((R.parent/'reference-library/entries/constrained-web-flow.json').read_text())['image_reference_use']['recommended_reference_images']],'reference_selection_reason':'The source teaches the same constrained-context input/mechanism/outcome relationship; its inspected model-first reveal corrects the earlier inferred web-first order.','source_observations':b['source_reveal_order'],'state_images':[{**s,'image':'web-search/'+s['image']} for s in b['states']],'visual_approved_by_user':False,'generation_authorized_by_user':True,'layer_reconstruction':b['layer_reconstruction']}
(R/'storyboard.json').write_text(json.dumps({'mode':'reference-reconstruction','visual_workflow':'image-first','source_library_required':True,'audience':'Technical practitioners learning the reference explanation','scope':'One image-first design pilot, not another whole-video motion render','generation_authorization':'User explicitly requested generated graphic images and multiple storyboard images before motion.','scenes':[scene]},indent=2))
md=['# Image-first storyboard pilot','','The previous full-video graphic design was rejected. This pilot follows the revised process: narration → teaching purpose → master image → multiple keyframe images → visual review → editable reconstruction → motion.','','[Full process](PROCESS.md) · [Beat, rationale and layer blueprint](web-search/beat.json) · [Storyboard data](storyboard.json)','','## Reference and rejected baseline','','Source at 01:57:','','![Original reference](web-search/source-reference.png)','','Rejected reconstruction:','','![Rejected reconstruction](web-search/rejected-baseline.png)','','## Three proposed states','','Generated image direction for review. The first two images are derived from the same settled master; slight generative differences still require shared tokens in the editable reconstruction. No human visual approval is asserted.','']
for i,s in enumerate(b['states']):md += [f'### {i+1}. {s["id"].title()}',s['new_understanding'],f'![State {i+1}](web-search/{s["image"]})',f'**Narration:** {s["narration_role"]}',f'**Next motion:** {s["next_transition"]}','']
md += ['## Review notes','','The warm palette, serif labels, centered filled icons, shadows and fixed composition restore the intended direction. The model-card relative scale, exact label weight, gradient and shadows still need review against the original. The image-first checkpoint exists to resolve these before code and motion.','','The right tile reserves presenter space. Exact labels will be editable text. The source\'s “Accurate Results” applies to its constrained-context example, not all generic-model answers. A separate storyboard must explain the following business-context failure.','','## Next deliverable','','Reconstruct the chosen still as separate editable background/grid, surfaces, shadows, icons, labels and connectors. Compare the editable still first, then animate one explanation between the selected states with narration cues and reading holds.']
(R/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(md))
print('Image-first review and storyboard exported')
